### Current Experience

Currently if I want to use prisma `connectOrCreate` I need to write the raw object by myself.

```ts
roleService.createOne({
        name: "Manager",
        permissions: {
          connectOrCreate: { 
              // where permission model has @@unique[action, resource]
              create: { action: "View", resource: "Order" },
              where: { action: "View", resource: "Order" } 
           }
        }
  })
```

PS: roleService is extending [Base Service](https://www.arkosjs.com/docs/core-concepts/components/services#baseservice-for-prisma-models)

### Improved Experience

I think it would be better if I could only do:

```ts
roleService.createOne({
        name: "Manager",
        permissions: {
           // where permission model has @@unique[action, resource]
           action: "View",
           resource: "Order",
           apiAction: "connectOrCreate"
        }
     }
  })
```

And internally the [handleRelationFieldsInBody](https://github.com/Uanela/arkos/blob/e1a39f7862e0364ad9d956dba25526e4003351da/packages/arkos/src/modules/base/utils/helpers/base.service.helpers.ts#L93) would simply solve this.

